cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the manuscript it accompanies."
title: "wendling-dynamic-gains: dynamic synaptic gains in a Wendling neural mass model"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB code reproducing the figures of a study in which the excitatory, slow dendritic inhibitory and
  fast somatic inhibitory gains of the four-population Wendling neural mass model are promoted from
  constants to state variables driven by a three-state hysteresis law. The repository maps the four
  clinical periods onto regions of a (Gs,Gf) parameter plane, verifies the readout against archetypes and
  threshold sweeps, anchors trajectory statistics on the collapse of the slow inhibitory gain, and
  reproduces the region boundaries as a bifurcation structure. A three-zone network built on the same
  column shows that propagation acts on the onset and not on the termination of a discharge.
type: software
